ch10 opening lines: ["Baldino's workshop, late into the night. Every bench is covered in wire.","n_baldino: Five stations. Five places where the project's old machines can still be made to talk: the mains under Citadel, the lighthouse transmitter, my mill on Zeelich, the bore on Desert Island, and Sefa's dome on the Hamalayi.","n_baldino: My relays: the test pair from my table, grown up and put on masts. When all five hear each other at once, the shaft's blast doors will hear them too.","n_baldino: Now the limits. Each relay needs a clear line to the others, so they go up high. Each runs on power from where it stands: water, wind, steam, light. And together they hold the signal only a minute, so every station needs a friend standing by.","n_hero: Then we need friends at five stations, and a way to reach them all.","n_baldino: Oh, and before I forget. Take this. My pulse tool: a little thunder in a box. It jams anything with gears or wires for a few seconds. Drones, automatons, mills, doors.","n_baldino: It does nothing at all to anything alive, and it needs a few seconds to recharge. Don't wave it at mites and expect miracles.","n_baldino: The way is already here. Listen.","n_heskradio: Hesk here! I got the council's message. The glider's moored on Zeelich, by the dock. I'll fly you anywhere with a flat bit of ground. Not into the shaft, mind. She's a glider, not a mole.","TOAST c10_toast_relays"]
